```
D01 - Suspicious LSASS Access (T1003.001).
Documentation of the S4 (behavioural) and S3 (artifact) Splunk searches.
Copy ONE search block at a time; the ``` ``` lines are Splunk inline comments.
Baseline (2026-10-18, sensor-validated): benign SYSTEM accessors at boot were
wininit.exe, csrss.exe, Sysmon64.exe (all 0x1FFFFF), suppressed by full path.
```

```S4 behavioural, UNTUNED: any process opening lsass with a read-capable mask (initial detection plus boot-time noise).```
index=endpoint source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=10 TargetImage="*lsass.exe"
| eval ga=upper(GrantedAccess)
| search ga IN ("0X1010","0X1410","0X1438","0X143A","0X1FFFFF","0X1F1FFF","0X1F3FFF")
| table _time host SourceImage GrantedAccess CallTrace

```S4 behavioural, TUNED: benign SYSTEM sources suppressed by full path. Over 2026-10-15: untuned 11 events (6 benign boot, 5 attack), tuned 5 events (A1, A2 x3, A4), 0 benign.```
index=endpoint source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=10 TargetImage="*lsass.exe"
| eval ga=upper(GrantedAccess)
| search ga IN ("0X1010","0X1410","0X1438","0X143A","0X1FFFFF","0X1F1FFF","0X1F3FFF")
| search NOT (SourceImage="C:\\Windows\\system32\\wininit.exe" OR SourceImage="C:\\Windows\\system32\\csrss.exe" OR SourceImage="C:\\Windows\\Sysmon64.exe")
| table _time host SourceImage GrantedAccess CallTrace

```S3 artifact: a dump file written to disk. Covers A3 (Task Manager), which S4 cannot see. EID 11 FileCreate names the creating process in Image (NOT SourceImage). The tool branch also matches a benign .dmp by these tools, so treat a hit as a lead to corroborate against the S4 access event (same host and process), not proof the dump is of lsass.```
index=endpoint source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=11 TargetFilename="*.dmp"
| search TargetFilename="*lsass*" OR Image IN ("*\\taskmgr.exe","*\\procdump.exe","*\\procdump64.exe","*\\rundll32.exe")
| table _time host Image TargetFilename
